From 38ffcb2e172b25bb90c3335104c8fe115d53e2fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 11:18:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 364/369] header: play-once APNG for the animated
 login/logout/set-password header

The mp4 approach could never work on the login page. httpd's PRE-AUTH
allowlist (httpd.c:1153 + the send_login_page gates) only exempts
.png/.svg/.jpg/.gif/.css - NOT .mp4 (nor .webp). An unauthenticated request
for the header .mp4 was bounced to the login page, so the <video> source
failed and only the poster PNG showed. Registering the mime handler (the
earlier iteration) was necessary but not sufficient - the auth gate still
blocked it.

Fix with zero firmware / zero pre-auth change: ship the animation as an
APNG (RT-96U_REAPER_Header_anim.png). It uses the .png extension - already
served pre-auth and already handled by the **.png mime entry - and APNG in
a plain <img> autoplays once and freezes on the last frame natively (no
<video>, no poster, no autoplay policy, no cached-404 trap). 480w @15fps,
~0.97 MB, full colour; fades in and freezes on the full RT-BE96U REAPER
wordmark.

  - www/images/RT-96U_REAPER_Header_anim.png: new APNG (the .mp4 removed)
  - Main_Login / Main_Password / Logout / Reaper_FirstBoot: <video> -> <img>
  - web.c: revert the now-dead **.mp4 mime handler (keep the static surface
    exactly as before - no hardening change)
  - httpd.c: revert the mp4 login-IP accounting clause
  - SEPARATE file from the static RT-96U_REAPER_Header.png, which the shell
    and dashboard header still use unanimated

Keep EXTENDNO at Reaper_v2.3.0 (owner: do not burn version numbers on the
failed mp4 iterations).
